"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 249, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 35, "prompt": "What does the doctor think is crucial for obesity?\nA cutting back on episodes of calorie consumption\nB inexpensive methods to keeping individuals engaged\nC tools that assist people to keep track by monitoring", "sourcePage": 245, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 249, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 36, "prompt": "What in the speaker’s vies is the reason for chronic kidney disease?\nA fluctuation in the body’s acid - base balance\nB unchecked consumption of an adverse diet\nC accumulated kidney damage due to ageing\nNow look at extract two.\n\nExtract 2: Questions 37 to 42\nYou hear a gastroenterologist called Catherine Frenette talking about new treatment options for\nliver cancer.\nYou now have 90 seconds to read questions 37-42.", "sourcePage": 245, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 249, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 37, "prompt": "Why does the interviewer describe the numbers as shocking\nA incidence has been hugely higher in the past decade\nB unresectable liver cancer was detected in the past decade\nC underlying liver conditions mutated into liver cancer", "sourcePage": 246, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 249, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 38, "prompt": "How does Dr Frenette see alcohol-induced cirrhosis leading to liver cancer\nA reducing it should be a primary focus on the fight against liver cancer\nB fatty liver developed from alcoholism is leading to more liver cancer\nC unlike popular perception, alcoholism is not the leading trigger factor", "sourcePage": 246, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 249, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 39, "prompt": "Why are most liver cancers treated by liver doctors and not cancer doctors?\nA there are not many treatment options available for liver cancers yet\nB liver cancers typically have an underlying liver condition behind it\nC the best treatment options are surgical including transplantations", "sourcePage": 246, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 249, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 40, "prompt": "Why is it harder to diagnose liver cancer unlike other cancers?\nA the symptoms are all over the place and hence not possible to diagnose\nB liver conditions reveal fewer symptoms until they have progressed much\nC they symptoms for liver diseases and liver cancer are radically varied", "sourcePage": 246, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 249, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 41, "prompt": "How does the doctor regard liver function test?\nA she considers it to be simple lab test that should be done more often\nB she feels that test reports can sometimes be confusing and is unreliable\nC she is critical about primary care doctors not conducting the test annually", "sourcePage": 247, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 249, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 42, "prompt": "Why does the doctor think that liver cancer doesn’t get the attention despite being a major\nconcern?\nA patients do not present due to the social stigma associated with liver problems\nB liver cancer is ranked the fifth most common cause of cancer related deaths\nC it is one of the few cancer deaths that is contrastingly increasing in frequency\nYou now have two minutes to check your answers.\nTHAT IS THE END OF THE LISTENING TEST", "sourcePage": 247, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 249, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}], "skills": ["liste